The problem:
  - We want to create faster, more functional websites.
    we're trying to do more and more with Javascript.
    - Offload tasks from the server to the web browser.
        You're not paying for the cpu or bandwidth.
    - Better user experience:
        more responsive,
        non-web things like drag-and-drop.

  - BUT: Javascript is a pain
    (picture of a messed up website on IE)
    - browser incompatibilities
      - IE is the big stinker here.
        - Most of us can't afford to just ignore it.
        - There are more and more browsers out there.
          - You can't just support IE, Firefox, and maybe Safari.
            - Now there is iPhone, iPad, Android, other tablets....

    - Ajax is tricker: asynchronous, lots of typing, callbacks.

jQuery:
